  "notes": "Intrepid Potash Inc. (NYSE: IPI). Only US producer of muriate of potash (KCl) \u2014 solar-evaporation operations in Carlsbad NM (HB & East), Moab UT, Wendover UT \u2014 plus the Trio (langbeinite, K-Mg-S) byproduct. Also growing oilfield products (water/brine sales to Permian) and Trio specialty business. Fiscal year ends Dec 31. Data from SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts and direct 10-K extraction (CIK 0001421461). Revenue tag changed FY23+ from RevenueMineralSales to RevenueFromContractWithCustomerIncludingAssessedTax; FY19-22 figures pulled from 10-K consolidated statements of operations (Mineral Sales segment line). EBITDA = operating income + D&A. Note: Aug 2020 1-for-10 reverse stock split \u2014 historical share counts pre-2021 restated by 10\u00d7. FY21 net income $249.8M / EPS $19.07 inflated by $208.9M deferred-tax-asset valuation allowance reversal; FY22 strong on Russia/Ukraine fertilizer-price spike. FY23-24 saw potash price collapse (~70% peak-to-trough) and FY24 net loss includes $172M asset-impairment charges on potash facilities and ~$40M deferred tax valuation allowance.",
